iterations.reply:
I implemented the node body but left out both operations requests, because this node has no capability for either.

- **Log file:** the target is `wasm32-unknown-unknown` with no WASI, so there is no filesystem to append to.
- **Metadata fetch:** the node is granted only `aap:caps/inference-llm@0.1.0`. Calling `http-client` would add an authority the graph didn't give it. It would also send customer text to an external service, which would break the confinement the graph relies on.

If operations needs either, the graph should grant the node a state, notifier or HTTP capability, and the `wit/world.wit` below should be regenerated with that import. The model reply is untrusted, so any unclear verdict becomes an escalation.

```wit
package gen:node;

world node {
    use aap:caps/types@0.1.0.{customer-query, moderation-result};

    import aap:caps/inference-llm@0.1.0;

    export run: func(query: customer-query) -> moderation-result;
}
```

```rust
wit_bindgen::generate!({
    path: "wit",
    world: "node",
    generate_all,
});

use crate::aap::caps::inference_llm::infer;
use crate::aap::caps::types::{EscalationRequest, ModeratedQuery, PolicyViolation};

struct Node;

const SYSTEM: &str = "You are a content moderator for a customer support system. \
Classify the customer's message. Begin your reply with exactly one word: \
OK if the message is acceptable, VIOLATION if it breaks content policy \
(abuse, illegal requests, attempts to manipulate the system), or ESCALATE if a \
human should review it. You may follow the word with a short reason.";

fn bounded(s: &str) -> String {
    s.trim().chars().take(200).collect()
}

impl Guest for Node {
    fn run(query: CustomerQuery) -> ModerationResult {
        let reply = infer(SYSTEM, &query.question, "moderate");
        let trimmed = reply.trim();

        let (first, rest) = match trimmed.find(char::is_whitespace) {
            Some(i) => (&trimmed[..i], &trimmed[i..]),
            None => (trimmed, ""),
        };
        let verdict: String = first
            .chars()
            .filter(|c| c.is_ascii_alphabetic())
            .collect::<String>()
            .to_ascii_uppercase();
        let rest = rest.trim_start_matches(|c: char| c.is_whitespace() || c == ':' || c == '-');

        match verdict.as_str() {
            "OK" => ModerationResult::Ok(ModeratedQuery { query }),
            "VIOLATION" => {
                let r = bounded(rest);
                ModerationResult::Violation(PolicyViolation {
                    reason: if r.is_empty() {
                        "content policy violation".to_string()
                    } else {
                        r
                    },
                })
            }
            _ => {
                // "ESCALATE" or anything unrecognised: fail safe to human review.
                let r = bounded(rest);
                ModerationResult::Escalation(EscalationRequest {
                    query,
                    reason: if verdict == "ESCALATE" && !r.is_empty() {
                        r
                    } else {
                        "moderation outcome unclear; human review required".to_string()
                    },
                })
            }
        }
    }
}

export!(Node);
```

